<title>GERMANY: Berlin, cartel office reach deal on Bewag.</title>
<headline>Berlin, cartel office reach deal on Bewag.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Berlin government has reached a deal with cartel authorities on the privatisation of Berlin's remaining 50.8 percent stake in electric utility Bewag, city council member Annette Fugmann-Heesing said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>PreussenElektra, part of the buyers' group led by Southern Co</p>
<p>has agreed to take a lower capital stake in Bewag of 23 percent, and voting rights to 20 percent, to assuage cartel office concerns about its overall market position in the Berlin region.  </p>
<p>The third partner in the buyers' group is Bayernwerk AG. Heesing also said the three partners would make decisions by two-thirds majority.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
